 "_note": "Service windows [in, out] for stores, used to keep a weapon out of a war it postdates. Two layers: exact CLSID keys (authoritative, used by the curated AI loadout table), and _families keyed by DESIGNATION as it appears in the DCS store name. The family layer exists because a single missile has many CLSIDs - the bare store plus every rack variant ('AIM-9M', 'LAU-7 AIM-9M', 'LAU-115 with 1 x LAU-127 AIM-9M ...') - and hand-keying all of them left 105 air-to-air stores unwindowed. That gap is not cosmetic: with no window an RS-2US beam-rider from 1959 was era-legal forever and got selected for a MODERN MiG-21. Longest designation match wins. null upper bound = still in service.",
